From 6aea595c5a68ad95b933f1659d7248b0c36247d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XCH27 <49464716+XCH27@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:17:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Third-party plugins run MCP servers and hooks only after
 approval of exactly what they declare (OV-100 phase 3)

A package installed from a third-party marketplace keeps its skills and
commands, but its MCP servers and hooks wait until the person allows the
declared surface; the grant records a fingerprint of the MCP launch
definitions and hook commands, so an update that changes them asks again.
Built-in, official and person-declared folders are unchanged. The first
discovery without a grant store records enabled third-party packages as
existing installs, and install creates the store first, so upgrading never
stops a working plugin while new ones ask. Revocation reaches resident
Sessions through the shared availability check. Settings rows show Needs
approval with a review dialog listing what will run, and a revoke action.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
